#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

if (( $# != 0 )); then
    printf 'Usage: plan-linked-recall\n' >&2
    exit 2
fi

cat <<'PLAN'
Owner-run linked Variax recall plan (see run-linked-recall)

Start on saved PODxt channel 5B with Variax control enabled.
The backup identifies 5B as F-T-Model 1 and 1B as F-Chime 1.

1. Read the connected Variax 600. Confirm the baseline matches F-T-Model 1.
2. Select PODxt channel 1B from 5B and verify the PODxt readback.
3. Read the Variax 600 again. Confirm that it recalled F-Chime 1.
4. Return the PODxt to 5B, including if the target guitar read fails.
5. Read the Variax 600 again and compare its metadata with the baseline.

Keep the five captures together. The guitar checks compare preset metadata
apart from the live tone-knob field. Both channels are already saved.
PLAN
